{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Then I was astonished</b> — I was astonished for one hour." "<b>My lord</b> — my master." "<b>To set the heart</b> — like: ויהי עריך, and this is the way of instruction with the king. And some say: that his heart was toward HaShem, and there is no need, for it is correct in its plain sense."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:51.854697509Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}